Telemetry (on by default, unchanged from upstream)
--------------------------------------------------
The setting ENABLE_NEKRO_CLOUD ("Enable NekroAI cloud service") defaults to true. While it is
on, the application sends an hourly usage report (instance ID derived from environment
information, plugin-compatibility version, Docker flag, basic system information including the hostname,
and aggregate counts of users, channels, messages and sandbox executions; no chat or code
content) to https://cloud.nekro.ai, a service operated by the upstream project. This edition does not change
that behaviour.

To turn it off: set ENABLE_NEKRO_CLOUD to false (web UI: Settings > Basic settings; the setup
wizard; or <data directory>/configs/nekro-agent.yaml). Known limitation: when no NekroAI cloud
API key is configured, the telemetry report does not check that switch. To stop the reports for
certain, also set the environment variable NEKRO_NEKRO_CLOUD_API_BASE_URL (two NEKRO_ prefixes)
to an unreachable address such as http://127.0.0.1:9, or block cloud.nekro.ai at your egress
firewall; this also disables the cloud features. Details: README.md / README_en.md.

